WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.620
Cyanide is highly toxic.

2
00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:06.060
Yet chemists still use it
to build bigger molecules.

3
00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:10.740
With propanone, cyanide adds across
the carbon to oxygen double bond.

4
00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:13.060
The chain grows by one carbon.

5
00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:16.300
But an alkene's carbon
to carbon double bond?

6
00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:17.940
Cyanide leaves it alone.

7
00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:19.340
Two double bonds.

8
00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:22.720
So why does cyanide attack
one, and ignore the other?

9
00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:27.960
In this mission, you'll tell aldehydes
from ketones, and reduce both to alcohols.

10
00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:33.740
Then you'll follow cyanide's attack on a
carbonyl group, one curly arrow at a time.

11
00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:38.040
Your mission: explain why cyanide
adds to a carbonyl double bond,

12
00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:39.630
but not to an alkene. 